{"type":"text","timestamp":1792582712694,"sessionID":"ses_ea1c34da1ffeE7mN8rSviQJH53","part":{"id":"prt_15e4152830010ao8KoTxM10u8Y","messageID":"msg_15e410316001TsfBDbBRDVK6jN","sessionID":"ses_ea1c34da1ffeE7mN8rSviQJH53","type":"text","text":"\n\nSearch level passes with `work_ratio = 0.1837` — already better than the prior runs (s1: 0.289, s3: 0.256). Let me look at those prior candidates to understand the gap and see if there's a cheap win before I invest in an incremental repair.\n\n","time":{"start":1792582701699,"end":1792582712687}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792582712724,"sessionID":"ses_ea1c34da1ffeE7mN8rSviQJH53","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b273835101827713","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== s1 final candidate ===\"; cat /home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s1/candidate.py 2>/dev/null | head -120"},"output":"=== s1 final candidate ===\n\"\"\"Dynamic DFS forest maintenance from a fixed root (vertex 0).\n\nThe maintained forest is a valid DFS forest of the current directed graph\niff (Yang et al., Lemma 1) it has no forward-cross edge and its tree spans\nevery root-reachable vertex. A single edge flip breaks that invariant only\nin three cases:\n\n  1. insert u->v with u reachable and v not reachable\n       -> v (and possibly more) become reachable;\n  2. insert u->v with discover[u] < discover[v] and v not a descendant of u\n       -> a forward-cross edge is created;\n  3. delete u->v where u->v is a tree edge (parent[v] == u)\n       -> the subtree under v may detach.\n\nIn every other case the forest stays valid and we return it unchanged in\nO(1) (or O(out-degree) for the adjacency update). For the three breaking\ncases we re-run the DFS over the adjacency lists we maintain in state, which\nis O(n + m) -- cheaper than the O(n^2) full matrix scan of a recompute.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _full_dfs(n, adj):\n    \"\"\"Iterative DFS from root 0 over adjacency lists ``adj``.\n\n    Returns {'parent': list, 'discover': dict, 'finish': dict} where\n    discover/finish only contain reachable vertices and share one counter\n    starting at 0 (discover[0] == 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    parent = [None] * n\n    discover = {}\n    finish = {}\n    discover[0] = 0\n    timer = 1\n    stack = [(0, iter(adj[0]))]\n    while stack:\n        u, it = stack[-1]\n        pushed = False\n        for v in it:\n            if v not in discover:\n                parent[v] = u\n                discover[v] = timer\n                timer += 1\n                stack.append((v, iter(adj[v])))\n                pushed = True\n                break\n        if not pushed:\n            finish[u] = timer\n            timer += 1\n            stack.pop()\n    return {'parent': parent, 'discover': discover, 'finish': finish}\n\n\ndef _is_descendant(u, v, discover, finish):\n    \"\"\"v is a descendant of u iff discover[u] < discover[v] < finish[v] < finish[u].\"\"\"\n    return discover[u] < discover[v] < finish[v] < finish[u]\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for u in range(n):\n        row = graph[u]\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v]:\n                adj[u].append(v)\n    st = _full_dfs(n, adj)\n    st['adj'] = adj\n    return st\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    adj = state['adj']\n    adj[u].append(v)\n    discover = state['discover']\n    finish = state['finish']\n    if u not in discover:\n        # u not reachable: an edge out of it reaches no new vertex and\n        # cannot create a forward-cross edge among reachable vertices.\n        return state\n    if v not in discover:\n        # v (and possibly more) become reachable: re-search.\n        st = _full_dfs(len(adj), adj)\n        st['adj'] = adj\n        return st\n    # v reachable: only a forward-cross edge can break validity.\n    if discover[u] < discover[v] and not _is_descendant(u, v, discover, finish):\n        st = _full_dfs(len(adj), adj)\n        st['adj'] = adj\n        return st\n    return state\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    adj = state['adj']\n    adj[u].remove(v)\n    parent = state['parent']\n    discover = state['discover']\n    if v in discover and parent[v] == u:\n        # tree edge removed: the subtree under v may detach, re-search.\n        st = _full_dfs(len(adj), adj)\n        st['adj'] = adj\n        return st\n    # non-tree edge: the tree still spans every reachable vertex, so the\n    # forest stays valid.\n    return state\n","metadata":{"output":"=== s1 final candidate ===\n\"\"\"Dynamic DFS forest maintenance from a fixed root (vertex 0).\n\nThe maintained forest is a valid DFS forest of the current directed graph\niff (Yang et al., Lemma 1) it has no forward-cross edge and its tree spans\nevery root-reachable vertex. A single edge flip breaks that invariant only\nin three cases:\n\n  1. insert u->v with u reachable and v not reachable\n       -> v (and possibly more) become reachable;\n  2. insert u->v with discover[u] < discover[v] and v not a descendant of u\n       -> a forward-cross edge is created;\n  3. delete u->v where u->v is a tree edge (parent[v] == u)\n       -> the subtree under v may detach.\n\nIn every other case the forest stays valid and we return it unchanged in\nO(1) (or O(out-degree) for the adjacency update). For the three breaking\ncases we re-run the DFS over the adjacency lists we maintain in state, which\nis O(n + m) -- cheaper than the O(n^2) full matrix scan of a recompute.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _full_dfs(n, adj):\n    \"\"\"Iterative DFS from root 0 over adjacency lists ``adj``.\n\n    Returns {'parent': list, 'discover': dict, 'finish': dict} where\n    discover/finish only contain reachable vertices and share one counter\n    starting at 0 (discover[0] == 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    parent = [None] * n\n    discover = {}\n    finish = {}\n    discover[0] = 0\n    timer = 1\n    stack = [(0, iter(adj[0]))]\n    while stack:\n        u, it = stack[-1]\n        pushed = False\n        for v in it:\n            if v not in discover:\n                parent[v] = u\n                discover[v] = timer\n                timer += 1\n                stack.append((v, iter(adj[v])))\n                pushed = True\n                break\n        if not pushed:\n            finish[u] = timer\n            timer += 1\n            stack.pop()\n    return {'parent': parent, 'discover': discover, 'finish': finish}\n\n\ndef _is_descendant(u, v, discover, finish):\n    \"\"\"v is a descendant of u iff discover[u] < discover[v] < finish[v] < finish[u].\"\"\"\n    return discover[u] < discover[v] < finish[v] < finish[u]\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for u in range(n):\n        row = graph[u]\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v]:\n                adj[u].append(v)\n    st = _full_dfs(n, adj)\n    st['adj'] = adj\n    return st\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    adj = state['adj']\n    adj[u].append(v)\n    discover = state['discover']\n    finish = state['finish']\n    if u not in discover:\n        # u not reachable: an edge out of it reaches no new vertex and\n        # cannot create a forward-cross edge among reachable vertices.\n        return state\n    if v not in discover:\n        # v (and possibly more) become reachable: re-search.\n        st = _full_dfs(len(adj), adj)\n        st['adj'] = adj\n        return st\n    # v reachable: only a forward-cross edge can break validity.\n    if discover[u] < discover[v] and not _is_descendant(u, v, discover, finish):\n        st = _full_dfs(len(adj), adj)\n        st['adj'] = adj\n        return st\n    return state\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    adj = state['adj']\n    adj[u].remove(v)\n    parent = state['parent']\n    discover = state['discover']\n    if v in discover and parent[v] == u:\n        # tree edge removed: the subtree under v may detach, re-search.\n        st = _full_dfs(len(adj), adj)\n        st['adj'] = adj\n        return st\n    # non-tree edge: the tree still spans every reachable vertex, so the\n    # forest stays valid.\n    return state\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== s1 final candidate ===\"; cat /home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s1/candidate.py 2>/dev/null | head -120","time":{"start":1792582712707,"end":1792582712717}},"id":"prt_15e415422001rqRkBlC5M8v6pR","sessionID":"ses_ea1c34da1ffeE7mN8rSvi