{"type":"text","timestamp":1792583613700,"sessionID":"ses_ea1c34da1ffeE7mN8rSviQJH53","part":{"id":"prt_15e4f2ed1001mOq5WzrvA8nt0E","messageID":"msg_15e4f28c50013cRxxL0NngdHt6","sessionID":"ses_ea1c34da1ffeE7mN8rSviQJH53","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Done — final verdict: PASS\n\n**Run:** `eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s2` · workspace `/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s2`\n\n| Check | Level | Verdict | work_ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | examples (n≤3) | FAIL | — |\n| 2 | examples (n≤3) | PASS | — |\n| 3 | search (n≤4) | PASS | 0.184 |\n| 4 | **final (n≤5)** | **PASS** | **0.126** |\n\nFinal grade: 4,187,856 / 4,187,856 sequences correct, fitness 1.0. `evoalgo finish` recorded `harness_done`. Used 4 checks (budget was 8).\n\n**The idea (two lines):**\nA directed forest is a genuine DFS forest iff it has no forward-cross edge (Yang et al. Lemma 1). So each update is checked in O(1) against the stored discover/finish intervals: an insert only invalidates if it creates a forward-cross edge or makes a new vertex reachable, and a delete only invalidates if it removes a tree edge. Otherwise the state is returned unchanged; on the rare invalidating update a single iterative DFS recomputes the forest.\n\n**Why this beats prior runs:** the recompute is a pure-Python adjacency-matrix scan, which runs at ~half the wall-time of the numpy offline baseline, and ~64% of updates are no-ops. Result: 0.126 final vs. 0.272 (s1) and 0.290 (s3).\n\n**Decision on incremental repair:** I measured the invalidating cases (newly-reachable insert 14%, forward-cross insert 3.5%, tree-edge delete 19%). The newly-reachable case is not cleanly repairable locally — the new reachable set can include vertices only reachable via paths back through old vertices, so a local re-search misses them and would fail the reachability check. A correct repair needs a near-full recompute anyway, so it wasn't worth the risk against the check budget. Stopped at the baseline.\n\nScratch files cleaned (two `.nfs*` entries remain — NFS silly-rename artifacts from finished processes, reclaimed automatically by the kernel).","time":{"start":1792583610065,"end":1792583613694}}}
